The first adversary run found a real flaw: the residual greedy attack solved 8/8 instances. The large random square multipliers made each floor-square sequence so dense that greedy filling became exact—precisely the “large denominator becomes dense” easy regime noted in Section 1. I’m removing that scaling regime and keeping only small square factors, then growing the normalized arithmetic haystack instead.
